<h1>panels</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>There are common panes located to the left hand of the KUBE screen:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="Scan_Pane_(Arm_Menu).htm" target="_self">Scan Pane</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="Entities_Pane.htm">Entities Pane</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><a href="Output_Pane.htm">Output Pane</a></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet">Tool Pane - this pane is active when KUBE enters in a specific mode. It offers functionality depending on the currently active mode. Description of the Tool Pane can be found in the correspondent topics, for example Datum mode, Geometry\Fits, etc.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>All these panes are overlapped and you can switch between them by clicking on their tabs (which are in the lower left hand side) or by shortcuts (<span class="Shortcut">Ctrl + 1</span> for Scan pane, <span class="Shortcut">Ctrl + 2</span> for Entities pane, <span class="Shortcut">Ctrl + 3</span> for Output pane). As the Tool Pane is not always present, there is no default shortcut assigned to it.</p>
<p>When the KUBE software is started for the first time Scan Pane is shown by default</p>
